-- TEXT: the numeric str-edge above 2^53. The digits name an exact i64, but
-- the edge routes through a double and loses the low bit — 2^53+1 arrives as
-- 2^53. §12 B-13 makes this edge part of the declared contract, so a lossy
-- edge is a wrong answer rather than a rounding policy.
-- expect: 9007199254740992
main = (): i64
    b = to(i64)("9007199254740993")
    print("{b}")
    0
end
